CONTRIBUTION_TYPE: mechanism
SCALE_REALISM: insufficient evidence for realistic workload. The L0 is reproducible CPU simulation (`python3 sim.py && python3 analyze.py`, 64 seeds, 6400 rows) and appears to fix the prior circularity/baseline defects within that simulator, but it does not establish real tool-agent traces contain enough delayed cold-then-hot callbacks, does not use real model attention/KV behavior, and reports synthetic task-chain availability rather than end-to-end task success at GPU serving scale.
RATIONALE: PROMPT_VERSION v001. This is not killed by an exact shipping implementation: I found retention infrastructure (TensorRT-LLM token-range priority retention) and direct attention/KV baselines (H2O/SnapKV/Scissorhands), but not a shipped system that predicts delayed tool-result re-reference from noisy handle/ngram plus past-attention signals. However, the systems contribution is bounded: once a predictor exists, deployment largely maps scores to already-shipped priority-retention APIs, and the packet’s own evidence says CAUSAL ties H2O on aggregate availability, wins only on M2 where H2O/RT are 0, and loses/ties at tight budgets or crit_AUC≈0.588. Required next evidence: real LLM accumulated attention, real measured future-reference AUC on committed tool outputs, real AppWorld/OfficeBench/tau-bench-style task accuracy at matched KV/token budgets, and head-to-head against H2O/SnapKV/Scissorhands/ACON using a GPU artifact.
